-/goal {"kind":"Stage Goal Context","issue_identifier":"#37","title":"Accept Agent Context Snapshot Runtime Semantics","description":"## Specification\n\nSpec: `spec/spec-architecture-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md`\nADR: `docs/adr/0019-agent-context-snapshot-runtime-semantics.md`\nGlossary: `CONTEXT.md`\n\n## Accepted model\n\nAgent Context Snapshot and Context Command are Workspace Repository scoped, harness-level behaviors. Symphony generates bounded launch context in its own launch harness and must not install or mutate global Codex lifecycle hooks.\n\nOwnership boundaries:\n\n- Runtime Settings own operator-configurable Agent Context Snapshot and Context Command behavior.\n- Agent Prompt composition owns prompt injection.\n- Runtime State may expose live context generation status and bounded diagnostics references.\n- Ignored Runtime Diagnostics may store bounded, secret-free context metadata.\n\nPrompt semantics:\n\n- Agent Context Snapshot supplements the Agent Prompt.\n- Agent Context Snapshot supplements Stage Goal Handoff when both are enabled.\n- Agent Context Snapshot must not replace the Agent Prompt or Stage Goal Handoff.\n- Context Command stdout may supplement Agent Context Snapshot content.\n- Context Command stderr and failures remain diagnostic by default.\n\nConstraints:\n\n- Preserve existing Runtime Contract defaults unless the operator explicitly approves a default change.\n- Do not persist `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `GH_TOKEN`, local `.env` contents, full rendered Agent Prompts, or full Codex transcripts in Runtime Contract files.\n- Use precise terms such as Agent Context Snapshot and Context Command; avoid ambiguous phrases such as \"full context\" and \"context compression\".\n\n## Documentation completed\n\n- [x] Added ADR under `docs/adr/` stating context generation happens in the Symphony launch harness, not through Codex lifecycle hooks.\n- [x] Defined which parts belong in Runtime Settings, Runtime State, Agent Prompt composition, and ignored Runtime Diagnostics.\n- [x] Stated that Agent Context Snapshot supplements the Agent Prompt and Stage Goal Handoff.\n- [x] Stated that Context Command stdout may supplement the Agent Prompt, while stderr and failures remain diagnostic by default.\n- [x] Updated `CONTEXT.md` with accepted terms and avoid-list wording for ambiguous phrases such as \"full context\" or \"context compression\".\n- [x] Preserved existing Runtime Contract defaults unless the operator explicitly approves a default change.\n\n## Blocked by\n\nNone - ready for implementation slices.\n\n---\ntitle: Agent Context Snapshot Runtime Semantics\nversion: 1.0\ndate_created: 2026-05-06\nlast_updated: 2026-05-06\nowner: Product Repository maintainers\ntags: [architecture, agent-context, runtime-contract, issue-37]\n---\n\n# Introduction\n\nThis specification defines the accepted runtime semantics for Agent Context Snapshot and Context Command behavior in Personal Symphony.\n\nSource issue: [#37 Accept Agent Context Snapshot Runtime Semantics](https://github.com/MatheusBBarni/symphony-orchestrator/issues/37).\n\n## 1. Purpose & Scope\n\nThe purpose is to define domain language and architecture boundaries before implementation changes Runtime Settings, Runtime State, Agent Prompt composition, or Runtime Home diagnostics.\n\nThis specification applies to the Product Repository implementation and to Workspace Repository Runtime Contract behavior.\n\nOut of scope:\n\n- Implementing Context Command execution.\n- Implementing independent stage completion review.\n- Installing or mutating global Codex lifecycle hooks.\n\n## 2. Definitions\n\n- **Workspace Repository**: The repository where the operator runs Personal Symphony.\n- **Product Repository**: The Personal Symphony source repository.\n- **Runtime Home**: The `.symphony/` directory in a Workspace Repository.\n- **Runtime Contract**: Repository-owned Runtime Home files that define Personal Symphony behavior.\n- **Runtime Settings**: The `.symphony/settings.json` portion of the Runtime Contract.\n- **Runtime State**: Ignored Runtime Home files and backend snapshots that record current orchestration activity.\n- **Agent Prompt**: The rendered task instruction sent to an agent.\n- **Stage Goal Handoff**: A stage-specific Codex handoff that sets a Codex goal before the normal Agent Prompt.\n- **Agent Context Snapshot**: A bounded, deterministic context section generated by the Symphony launch harness before agent launch or retry.\n- **Context Command**: An optional operator-configured local command whose bounded stdout may supplement Agent Context Snapshot content.\n\n## 3. Requirements, Constraints & Guidelines\n\n- **REQ-001**: Agent Context Snapshot MUST be generated by the Symphony launch harness.\n- **REQ-002**: Agent Context Snapshot MUST be scoped to the active Workspace Repository.\n- **REQ-003**: Agent Context Snapshot MUST supplement, not replace, the Agent Prompt.\n- **REQ-004**: Agent Context Snapshot MUST coexist with Stage Goal Handoff.\n- **REQ-005**: Runtime Settings MUST own operator-configurable context behavior.\n- **REQ-006**: Runtime State MAY expose context generation status and bounded diagnostics.\n- **REQ-007**: Ignored Runtime Home diagnostics MAY store bounded metadata about context generation.\n- **REQ-008**: `CONTEXT.md` MUST define accepted context terminology.\n- **CON-001**: The implementation MUST NOT install or mutate global Codex lifecycle hooks.\n- **CON-002**: The implementation MUST NOT store full Codex transcripts in the Runtime Contract.\n- **CON-003**: The implementation MUST NOT persist `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `GH_TOKEN`, or local `.env` contents.\n- **GUD-001**: Use precise names such as Agent Context Snapshot and Context Command instead of ambiguous phrases such as \"full context.\"\n\n## 4. Interfaces & Data Contracts\n\n### Runtime Ownership\n\n| Concern | Owner | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Enablement and limits | Runtime Settings | User-editable Runtime Contract. |\n| Prompt injection | Agent Prompt composition | Generated immediately before launch. |\n| Live status | Runtime State | Exposed to CLI/server/dashboard snapshots. |\n| Debug metadata | Ignored Runtime Home diagnostics | Bounded and secret-free. |\n| Domain terms | `CONTEXT.md` | Source of truth for glossary. |\n\n### ADR Requirements\n\nAny accepted runtime semantic change MUST be documented in `docs/adr/`.\n\n## 5. Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **AC-001**: Given implementation begins, When runtime context semantics are introduced, Then an ADR exists under `docs/adr/`.\n- **AC-002**: Given `CONTEXT.md` is reviewed, When Agent Context Snapshot and Context Command are used, Then the terms are defined there.\n- **AC-003**: Given Stage Goal Handoff is enabled, When Agent Context Snapshot is enabled, Then both mechanisms remain distinct and ordered.\n- **AC-004**: Given Runtime Contract files are inspected, When diagnostics are generated, Then full prompts and secret values are absent.\n\n## 6. Test Automation Strategy\n\n- **Test Levels**: Documentation validation and backend tests in implementation slices.\n- **Frameworks**: OCaml Alcotest for backend behavior.\n- **Test Data Management**: Use temporary Workspace Repository fixtures.\n- **CI/CD Integration**: Run `pnpm test` after implementation slices.\n- **Coverage Requirements**: Each runtime semantic implemented later must have focused tests.\n- **Performance Testing**: Not required for this design slice.\n\n## 7. Rationale & Context\n\n`codex-loop` uses Codex lifecycle hooks for continuation. Symphony already owns agent launch, Agent Worktrees, prompt writing, retries, and Runtime State. Therefore, the transferable design is harness-level bounded context generation, not global hook installation.\n\n## 8. Dependencies & External Integrations\n\n### External Systems\n\n- **EXT-001**: GitHub Issues + Projects - Supplies issue metadata and stage state.\n- **EXT-002**: Git - Supplies branch and worktree state.\n\n### Infrastructure Dependencies\n\n- **INF-001**: Runtime Home - Stores Runtime Contract, Runtime State, and diagnostics.\n\n### Technology Platform Dependencies\n\n- **PLT-001**: OCaml backend - Owns settings parsing, prompt composition, and orchestration.\n\n### Compliance Dependencies\n\n- **COM-001**: ADR coverage - Required for runtime semantic changes.\n\n## 9. Examples & Edge Cases\n\n```text\nAgent Prompt\n---\nStage Goal Handoff content, when enabled\n---\nAgent Context Snapshot, when enabled\n```\n\nEdge cases:\n\n- Missing context settings means context behavior remains disabled.\n- Context diagnostics must not make Runtime Contract files non-idempotent.\n- Ambiguous domain terms must be rejected during documentation review.\n\n## 10. Validation Criteria\n\n- ADR exists and describes runtime ownership boundaries.\n- `CONTEXT.md` includes accepted terms and avoid-list wording.\n- Later implementation issues can reference this specification without redefining context semantics.\n\n## 11. Related Specifications / Further Reading\n\n- [Issue #37](https://github.com/MatheusBBarni/symphony-orchestrator/issues/37)\n- [CONTEXT.md](../CONTEXT.md)\n- [Codex Loop Context Management Analysis](../docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md)\n- [Stage Goal Handoff ADR](../docs/adr/0007-stage-goal-handoff.md)\n","comments":[{"author":"MatheusBBarni","body":"---\ntitle: Agent Context Snapshot Runtime Semantics\nversion: 1.0\ndate_created: 2026-05-06\nlast_updated: 2026-05-06\nowner: Product Repository maintainers\ntags: [architecture, agent-context, runtime-contract, issue-37]\n---\n\n# Introduction\n\nThis specification defines the accepted runtime semantics for Agent Context Snapshot and Context Command behavior in Personal Symphony.\n\nSource issue: [#37 Accept Agent Context Snapshot Runtime Semantics](https://github.com/MatheusBBarni/symphony-orchestrator/issues/37).\n\n## 1. Purpose & Scope\n\nThe purpose is to define domain language and architecture boundaries before implementation changes Runtime Settings, Runtime State, Agent Prompt composition, or Runtime Home diagnostics.\n\nThis specification applies to the Product Repository implementation and to Workspace Repository Runtime Contract behavior.\n\nOut of scope:\n\n- Implementing Context Command execution.\n- Implementing independent stage completion review.\n- Installing or mutating global Codex lifecycle hooks.\n\n## 2. Definitions\n\n- **Workspace Repository**: The repository where the operator runs Personal Symphony.\n- **Product Repository**: The Personal Symphony source repository.\n- **Runtime Home**: The `.symphony/` directory in a Workspace Repository.\n- **Runtime Contract**: Repository-owned Runtime Home files that define Personal Symphony behavior.\n- **Runtime Settings**: The `.symphony/settings.json` portion of the Runtime Contract.\n- **Runtime State**: Ignored Runtime Home files and backend snapshots that record current orchestration activity.\n- **Agent Prompt**: The rendered task instruction sent to an agent.\n- **Stage Goal Handoff**: A stage-specific Codex handoff that sets a Codex goal before the normal Agent Prompt.\n- **Agent Context Snapshot**: A bounded, deterministic context section generated by the Symphony launch harness before agent launch or retry.\n- **Context Command**: An optional operator-configured local command whose bounded stdout may supplement Agent Context Snapshot content.\n\n## 3. Requirements, Constraints & Guidelines\n\n- **REQ-001**: Agent Context Snapshot MUST be generated by the Symphony launch harness.\n- **REQ-002**: Agent Context Snapshot MUST be scoped to the active Workspace Repository.\n- **REQ-003**: Agent Context Snapshot MUST supplement, not replace, the Agent Prompt.\n- **REQ-004**: Agent Context Snapshot MUST coexist with Stage Goal Handoff.\n- **REQ-005**: Runtime Settings MUST own operator-configurable context behavior.\n- **REQ-006**: Runtime State MAY expose context generation status and bounded diagnostics.\n- **REQ-007**: Ignored Runtime Home diagnostics MAY store bounded metadata about context generation.\n- **REQ-008**: `CONTEXT.md` MUST define accepted context terminology.\n- **CON-001**: The implementation MUST NOT install or mutate global Codex lifecycle hooks.\n- **CON-002**: The implementation MUST NOT store full Codex transcripts in the Runtime Contract.\n- **CON-003**: The implementation MUST NOT persist `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `GH_TOKEN`, or local `.env` contents.\n- **GUD-001**: Use precise names such as Agent Context Snapshot and Context Command instead of ambiguous phrases such as \"full context.\"\n\n## 4. Interfaces & Data Contracts\n\n### Runtime Ownership\n\n| Concern | Owner | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Enablement and limits | Runtime Settings | User-editable Runtime Contract. |\n| Prompt injection | Agent Prompt composition | Generated immediately before launch. |\n| Live status | Runtime State | Exposed to CLI/server/dashboard snapshots. |\n| Debug metadata | Ignored Runtime Home diagnostics | Bounded and secret-free. |\n| Domain terms | `CONTEXT.md` | Source of truth for glossary. |\n\n### ADR Requirements\n\nAny accepted runtime semantic change MUST be documented in `docs/adr/`.\n\n## 5. Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **AC-001**: Given implementation begins, When runtime context semantics are introduced, Then an ADR exists under `docs/adr/`.\n- **AC-002**: Given `CONTEXT.md` is reviewed, When Agent Context Snapshot and Context Command are used, Then the terms are defined there.\n- **AC-003**: Given Stage Goal Handoff is enabled, When Agent Context Snapshot is enabled, Then both mechanisms remain distinct and ordered.\n- **AC-004**: Given Runtime Contract files are inspected, When diagnostics are generated, Then full prompts and secret values are absent.\n\n## 6. Test Automation Strategy\n\n- **Test Levels**: Documentation validation and backend tests in implementation slices.\n- **Frameworks**: OCaml Alcotest for backend behavior.\n- **Test Data Management**: Use temporary Workspace Repository fixtures.\n- **CI/CD Integration**: Run `pnpm test` after implementation slices.\n- **Coverage Requirements**: Each runtime semantic implemented later must have focused tests.\n- **Performance Testing**: Not required for this design slice.\n\n## 7. Rationale & Context\n\n`codex-loop` uses Codex lifecycle hooks for continuation. Symphony already owns agent launch, Agent Worktrees, prompt writing, retries, and Runtime State. Therefore, the transferable design is harness-level bounded context generation, not global hook installation.\n\n## 8. Dependencies & External Integrations\n\n### External Systems\n\n- **EXT-001**: GitHub Issues + Projects - Supplies issue metadata and stage state.\n- **EXT-002**: Git - Supplies branch and worktree state.\n\n### Infrastructure Dependencies\n\n- **INF-001**: Runtime Home - Stores Runtime Contract, Runtime State, and diagnostics.\n\n### Technology Platform Dependencies\n\n- **PLT-001**: OCaml backend - Owns settings parsing, prompt composition, and orchestration.\n\n### Compliance Dependencies\n\n- **COM-001**: ADR coverage - Required for runtime semantic changes.\n\n## 9. Examples & Edge Cases\n\n```text\nAgent Prompt\n---\nStage Goal Handoff content, when enabled\n---\nAgent Context Snapshot, when enabled\n```\n\nEdge cases:\n\n- Missing context settings means context behavior remains disabled.\n- Context diagnostics must not make Runtime Contract files non-idempotent.\n- Ambiguous domain terms must be rejected during documentation review.\n\n## 10. Validation Criteria\n\n- ADR exists and describes runtime ownership boundaries.\n- `CONTEXT.md` includes accepted terms and avoid-list wording.\n- Later implementation issues can reference this specification without redefining context semantics.\n\n## 11. Related Specifications / Further Reading\n\n- [Issue #37](https://github.com/MatheusBBarni/symphony-orchestrator/issues/37)\n- [CONTEXT.md](../CONTEXT.md)\n- [Codex Loop Context Management Analysis](../docs/agent-context/codex-loop-context-management.md)\n- [Stage Goal Handoff ADR](../docs/adr/0007-stage-goal-handoff.md)\n","created_at":"2026-05-06T03:24:48Z","url":"https://github.com/MatheusBBarni/symphony-orchestrator/issues/37#issuecomment-4384841067"}],"url":"https://github.com/MatheusBBarni/symphony-orchestrator/issues/37","current_project_status":"In Review","labels":["enhancement","post alpha"],"priority":null,"blocker_references":[],"attempt":0,"stage_agent_name":"reviewer"}
+/goal {"kind":"Stage Goal Context","issue_identifier":"#38","title":"Inject A Built-In Agent Context Snapshot","description":"## What to build\n\nAdd a narrow, opt-in Agent Context Snapshot path for agent launches. When enabled for a matching Stage Agent, Symphony should append a deterministic bounded markdown snapshot to the composed Agent Prompt before launching the agent in its Agent Worktree.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Parse a stage-specific Runtime Settings shape for built-in context snapshots with missing config treated as disabled.\n- [ ] Validate invalid stage context config as a Readiness Gap before dispatch.\n- [ ] Render issue identifier, title, current project status, labels, blockers, attempt, Stage Agent name, Task Branch, Agent Worktree path, and Loop-Start Branch when available.\n- [ ] Append the snapshot under a stable heading after stage agent instructions and Stage Goal Handoff content.\n- [ ] Keep output ordering deterministic and enforce a max-size cap.\n- [ ] Add backend tests near existing config and prompt-composition coverage for disabled config, enabled config, invalid config, Stage Goal Handoff coexistence, and truncation.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #37\n\n# SPEC\n\n---\ntitle: Built-In Agent Context Snapshot\nversion: 1.0\ndate_created: 2026-05-06\nlast_updated: 2026-05-06\nowner: Product Repository maintainers\ntags: [design, agent-context, prompt-composition, issue-38]\n---\n\n# Introduction\n\nThis specification defines the built-in Agent Context Snapshot rendered into an Agent Prompt before Symphony launches a Stage Agent.\n\nSource issue: [#38 Inject A Built-In Agent Context Snapshot](https://github.com/MatheusBBarni/symphony-orchestrator/issues/38).\n\n## 1. Purpose & Scope\n\nThe purpose is to provide deterministic, bounded launch context without relying on Codex lifecycle hooks or full transcript storage.\n\nThis specification covers Runtime Settings parsing, readiness validation, prompt composition, snapshot content, ordering, and backend tests.\n\nOut of scope:\n\n- Retry stdout/stderr tails. Covered by issue #39.\n- Context Command execution. Covered by issue #40.\n- Dashboard display. Covered by issue #41.\n\n## 2. Definitions\n\n- **Stage Agent**: A configured agent mapped to one or more issue states.\n- **Agent Context Snapshot**: Bounded deterministic markdown appended to the Agent Prompt.\n- **Readiness Gap**: A pre-dispatch configuration problem surfaced to the operator.\n- **Task Branch**: A branch created for one dispatched issue.\n- **Agent Worktree**: The per-task Git worktree under Runtime Home.\n- **Loop-Start Branch**: The branch checked out when orchestration starts.\n- **Stage Goal Handoff**: Optional Codex goal handoff sent before the Agent Prompt.\n\n## 3. Requirements, Constraints & Guidelines\n\n- **REQ-001**: Missing snapshot configuration MUST mean disabled.\n- **REQ-002**: Enabled configuration MUST be stage-specific.\n- **REQ-003**: Invalid configuration MUST create a Readiness Gap before dispatch.\n- **REQ-004**: Snapshot rendering MUST include issue identifier, title, project status, labels, blockers, attempt, Stage Agent name, Task Branch, Agent Worktree path, and Loop-Start Branch when available.\n- **REQ-005**: Snapshot output MUST be deterministic in field order and list order.\n- **REQ-006**: Snapshot output MUST enforce a configured or default max-size cap.\n- **REQ-007**: Snapshot content MUST be appended under a stable markdown heading.\n- **REQ-008**: Snapshot rendering MUST coexist with Stage Goal Handoff and stage agent instructions.\n- **CON-001**: Snapshot rendering MUST NOT mutate Runtime Contract files.\n- **CON-002**: Snapshot rendering MUST NOT include secret environment values.\n- **GUD-001**: Snapshot field names SHOULD match `CONTEXT.md` domain terms.\n\n## 4. Interfaces & Data Contracts\n\n### Candidate Runtime Settings Shape\n\n```json\n{\n  \"stageAgents\": {\n    \"stages\": [\n      {\n        \"states\": [\"Todo\"],\n        \"agent\": \"engineer\",\n        \"context\": {\n          \"snapshot\": {\n            \"enabled\": true,\n            \"maxOutputBytes\": 12000\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Prompt Section\n\n```md\n## Agent Context Snapshot\n\n- Issue: #38 Inject A Built-In Agent Context Snapshot\n- Project status: Todo\n- Attempt: 1\n- Stage Agent: engineer\n- Task Branch: symphony/task/38-inject-a-built-in-agent-context-snapshot\n- Agent Worktree: .symphony/workspaces/...\n- Loop-Start Branch: symphony/dogfood\n```\n\n## 5. Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **AC-001**: Given no context config, When an agent launches, Then no Agent Context Snapshot is appended.\n- **AC-002**: Given valid enabled config, When an agent launches, Then the Agent Prompt includes the stable Agent Context Snapshot section.\n- **AC-003**: Given invalid config, When readiness is evaluated, Then a Readiness Gap identifies the stage and setting path.\n- **AC-004**: Given Stage Goal Handoff is enabled, When the prompt is composed, Then Stage Goal Handoff remains ordered before the normal Agent Prompt and snapshot content.\n- **AC-005**: Given large snapshot data, When rendering occurs, Then output is truncated deterministically.\n\n## 6. Test Automation Strategy\n\n- **Test Levels**: Backend unit and integration tests.\n- **Frameworks**: OCaml Alcotest.\n- **Test Data Management**: Use temporary config JSON, issues, and workspaces.\n- **CI/CD Integration**: Run `pnpm test`.\n- **Coverage Requirements**: Disabled config, enabled config, invalid config, ordering, truncation, and Stage Goal Handoff coexistence.\n- **Performance Testing**: Validate bounded rendering; no load test required.\n\n## 7. Rationale & Context\n\nAgents need enough local state to continue work after dispatch and retry. A built-in snapshot gives repeatable context without allowing unbounded transcript replay or hidden global Codex hook behavior.\n\n## 8. Dependencies & External Integrations\n\n### External Systems\n\n- **EXT-001**: GitHub Issues + Projects - Supplies issue status, labels, and blockers.\n- **EXT-002**: Git - Supplies branch and worktree names.\n\n### Infrastructure Dependencies\n\n- **INF-001**: Runtime Home - Stores Agent Worktrees and Runtime State.\n\n### Technology Platform Dependencies\n\n- **PLT-001**: OCaml backend - Implements Config and Orchestrator behavior.\n\n## 9. Examples & Edge Cases\n\n```text\nOrder:\n1. Stage Goal Handoff, when enabled\n2. Stage agent instructions and skill load, when configured\n3. Rendered Agent Prompt\n4. Agent Context Snapshot\n```\n\nEdge cases:\n\n- Labels list is empty.\n- Blockers list is empty.\n- Task Branch is created during dispatch and was not available before workspace preparation.\n\n## 10. Validation Criteria\n\n- `pnpm test` passes.\n- Prompt snapshots are deterministic.\n- Readiness Gaps are actionable.\n- No generated `.res.js` files are touched.\n\n## 11. Related Specifications / Further Reading\n\n- [Issue #38](https://github.com/MatheusBBarni/symphony-orchestrator/issues/38)\n- [Issue #37](https://github.com/MatheusBBarni/symphony-orchestrator/issues/37)\n- [CONTEXT.md](../CONTEXT.md)\n- [Agent Context Architecture Notes](../docs/agent-context/architecture.md)\n","comments":[],"url":"https://github.com/MatheusBBarni/symphony-orchestrator/issues/38","current_project_status":"In Progress","labels":["enhancement"],"priority":null,"blocker_references":[],"attempt":0,"stage_agent_name":"engineer"}
 
